        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-accordion">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>What payment methods do you accept?</h3>
            <p>We accept cash, Zelle, Apple Cash, and all major credit cards. We do not accept CareCredit.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Are there any cancellation fees?</h3>
            <p>We understand that a pet's condition can change rapidly, or you may simply need more time. Cancellations made at least 24 hours in advance incur no fee. For same-day cancellations, a partial consultation fee may apply to cover the doctor's scheduled time.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Do you accept pet insurance or CareCredit?</h3>
            <p>We do not accept CareCredit and do not directly bill pet insurance. We can provide a detailed invoice that you may submit to your pet insurance provider for possible reimbursement.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Is there an extra charge for weekend or after-hours visits?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Appointments scheduled outside of our standard operating hours (evenings, weekends, and holidays) generally incur an emergency/after-hours fee, typically ranging from $50 to $100. We will inform you of this when you call.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Are there options for free dog euthanasia in Los Angeles?</h3>
            <p>As a private mobile veterinary practice, we do not offer free dog euthanasia services. However, if you are facing severe financial hardship, we recommend reaching out to local non-profit animal shelters or humane societies in Los Angeles or your local county, as they sometimes offer low-cost or free compassionate services at their clinics.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

